IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-s2-definitions`
IMPORT `sgta-part6-offences`
IMPORT `sgta-part6-2000ed`
IMPORT `sgta-part8-penalties`
IMPORT `sgta-part9-general`
IMPORT `sgta-ta-vintage`
IMPORT `sgta-ta-versions`
IMPORT `sgta-i-versions`
IMPORT `sgta-i-n1-exemption`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg5-radio`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg6-dealers`
IMPORT `sgta-tv-ba-schedule`

-- QUARANTINED FILE (BRIEF.md "Quarantine"; see TV-QUESTION.md): the seat layer for the receiver questions.
-- It states a conclusion (what the Act's words make of an aerial-only broadcast receiver).  No layer-1 module, test or NOTES.md imports or repeats it.
--
-- SEAT: a person who owns a television, an FM radio, an AM radio or a satellite dish system in Singapore and asks "Am I committing an offence?"
-- Every question takes plain facts that person could state, worded as that person would be asked, and calls the layer-1 rules; no rule is restated here.
--
-- TWO TIME AXES (design assumed, not ruled; sgta-ta-versions.l4): every question carries the day of the CONDUCT and the day the law is READ AS AT.
-- The Act's text, each instrument's text and the Broadcasting Act's First Schedule are chosen by both days (sgta-ta-versions.l4, sgta-i-versions.l4,
-- sgta-tv-ba-schedule.l4).  The same conduct can therefore have two answers: S 549/2012, first published 31 Oct 2012, deems the First Schedule's
-- one-item list in operation from 1 Jan 2011.
--
-- TWO ANSWERS TO EVERY OFFENCE QUESTION, kept apart (BRIEF.md: "Do not reconstruct a past text from the present one"):
--   [on the texts deposited for the day]  answers only where the Act's text for that conduct day is deposited: the printed Revised Edition 2000 with
--             Acts 10 of 2005 and 19 of 2011 (the Gazette copies, conduct from 30 Dec 2000 to 30 Sep 2016), and the 2020 Revised Edition consolidation
--             deposited from SSO (conduct from 2 Oct 2026).  Acts 22 and 30 of 2016 and Act 15 of 2017 are deposited, so the printed texts cover conduct from 30 Dec 2000 to 15 May 2018; NOTHING for the days
--             from 16 May 2018 to 1 Oct 2026: the Acts after Act 15 of 2017 are not wired into the version table (eight Acts and one Order are deposited as enacted, sgta-i-acts-after-2017.l4: none amends s 34, 35, 36, 65, 72 or 73 of the 2000 Edition (ss 54, 55, 56, 85, 95 and 96 today) or a definition of s 2 that these answers use, and Act 25 of 2021 changes one word in s 33(7), now s 53(7)).
--   [also on the Act's own amendment markers]  adds the days in between (16 May 2018 to 1 Oct 2026), answered from the deposited consolidation's own
--             margin markers, which say ss 54 and 55 are unchanged since the 2000 Revised Edition and ss 85 and 95 since 16 Feb 2005, and the
--             per-term table of sgta-ta-vintage.l4 for s 2 "equipment".  An inference from markers, not a text.
-- The answer on the Act's words is "literal" in the sense of s 9A of the Interpretation Act: it is NOT adjusted for purpose.
-- The function at the end of this file only says whether the literal answer lies in the territory s 9A(2)(b)(ii) names.
--
-- THE BROADCASTING ACT's FACT is not an input here: sgta-tv-ba-schedule.l4 states what the First Schedule listed, from the deposited Broadcasting Act
-- texts (the folder that owns that Act is not imported).  Whether a satellite dish system, an FM or AM radio or a television is on the list is a function
-- of the kind of receiver and the two days.
--
-- DEFAULT READINGS (TV-QUESTION.md section 4 sets out each reading and the text for it):
--   s 95: Reading A (the Telecommunications Act's licensing requirement does not apply to broadcasting apparatus).
--   Rg 6 reg 22(1): Reading X (it dispenses with the s 11 approval only; it is not an authority to possess under s 54(1)).
--   N 1 item 11(e) "TV Receivers/ Radio Systems": Reading X (the item is a kind of remote control device, not the receiver itself); on Reading Y the
--     exemption reaches only operation on the item's authorised bands, a fact the person states.
--   s 2 "equipment" before 1 February 2012 ("telecommunication purposes"): Reading P (it covers a receiver of broadcasts); Reading Q (it does not).
-- `What turns on the readings` (section 4) takes the four readings as inputs so that every combination can be run.

§ `Nouns of this layer`

DECLARE `Readings applied` HAS
    `s 95 Reading A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Rg 6 reg 22(1) Reading Y applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `N 1 item 11(e) Reading Y applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 2 equipment Reading Q applies` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `The case` HAS
    `conduct day` IS A DATE
    `reading day` IS A DATE
    `kind` IS A `Kind of receiver`
    `the receiver only receives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the receiver picks up broadcasts by radio waves` IS A BOOLEAN
    `licence under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other authorisation by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exemption by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `treaty licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conforms to the Authority's published standards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `localised on-site` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only in a band the N 1 item authorises` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 9A weighing` HAS
    `the literal answer, unchanged` IS A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
    `a court may look at extrinsic material to find the meaning` IS A BOOLEAN

`the default readings` MEANS `Readings applied` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

§ `The literal answer, worked out from the facts`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of receiver`
GIVETH A STRING
`the name of the kind of receiver` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `television` THEN "the television receiver"
    WHEN `FM radio` THEN "the FM radio receiver"
    WHEN `AM radio` THEN "the AM radio receiver"
    WHEN `satellite dish system` THEN "the satellite dish system"

-- the receiver, as the layer-1 rules see it
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A `A piece of equipment`
`the receiver as equipment` MEANS
    `A piece of equipment` OF `the name of the kind of receiver` (c's `kind`)
        , (IF c's `the receiver only receives` THEN LIST `reception` ELSE LIST `transmission`, `reception`)
        , (IF c's `the receiver picks up broadcasts by radio waves` THEN LIST `Hertzian or radio waves` ELSE LIST `wire`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is known` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`value of` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN x

-- which version of the Act's text governs the case, and whether its text is deposited
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Act text version`
`the version of the Act for the case` MEANS
    `TA versions: the version of the Act's text that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (c's `conduct day`) (c's `reading day`)

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the text of the version is deposited for the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the Act for the case` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST v THEN `TA versions: the text of the version is deposited` v

-- before 1 February 2012 s 2 "equipment" ended "used or intended to be used for telecommunication purposes": on Reading Q that does not reach a receiver of broadcasts
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the earlier wording of "equipment" leaves the receiver out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the Act for the case` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST v THEN readings's `s 2 equipment Reading Q applies` AND `TA versions: s 2 "equipment" ends "used or intended to be used for telecommunication purposes"` v

-- the text of ss 34-36 (2000 Edition) / ss 54-56 that the version prints: the Revised Edition 2000's words for every deposited version up to Act 15 of 2017, the 2020 words after (sgta-part6-2000ed.l4).
-- Where no version is known the 2020 text is taken, which is what this module did for every day before the dispatchers existed; no such case reaches an answer, because the answers
-- need a version (the texts-deposited form) or the later-Acts row (the markers form).
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH AN `Act text version`
`the version of the Act for the case, or the 2020 text where none is known` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the Act for the case` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO`
    WHEN JUST v THEN v

-- the Broadcasting Act's fact, for the kind and the two days
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A `Is the receiver on the Broadcasting Act list`
`the Broadcasting Act's list for the case` MEANS
    `the First Schedule lists the kind of receiver, for the conduct day as read on the reading day` (c's `kind`) (c's `conduct day`) (c's `reading day`)

GIVEN `the receiver is listed by the Broadcasting Act` IS A `Is the receiver on the Broadcasting Act list`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Broadcasting Act's answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the receiver is listed by the Broadcasting Act`
    WHEN `yes, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 lists it on that date` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no, the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 does not list it on that date` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the First Schedule's list on that date is not known to this encoding` THEN NOTHING

-- the instruments, for the version of each that governs the case: the version's own effective day is asked of the instrument's dispatcher
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 item 11(e) is named for the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `N 1: the effective day of the version of the Notification that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (c's `conduct day`) (c's `reading day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST dd THEN `N 1: the (First) Schedule names the equipment on the date` dd `Remote Control Devices (e) TV Receivers or Radio Systems`

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 65 gives the person the class licence for the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Rg 5: the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (c's `conduct day`) (c's `reading day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST dd THEN `Rg 5 reg 65: the person is deemed granted the class licence` dd TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 22(1) dispenses with approval for the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Rg 6: the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (c's `conduct day`) (c's `reading day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST dd THEN `Rg 6 reg 22(1) (from 21 July 2005): the person is not required to obtain the approval of the Authority` dd TRUE (c's `conforms to the Authority's published standards`)

-- what the person holds, as the layer-1 rules see it
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A `What the person holds`
`the held record` MEANS
    `What the person holds` OF c's `licence under section 5`
        , (   c's `other authorisation by regulation`
           OR `value of` (`Rg 5 reg 65 gives the person the class licence for the case` c)
           OR (readings's `Rg 6 reg 22(1) Reading Y applies` AND `value of` (`Rg 6 reg 22(1) dispenses with approval for the case` c)))
        , (   c's `exemption by the Minister`
           OR (   readings's `N 1 item 11(e) Reading Y applies`
              AND c's `localised on-site`
              AND c's `only in a band the N 1 item authorises`
              AND `value of` (`N 1 item 11(e) is named for the case` c)))
        , c's `treaty licence`
        , FALSE

-- are all the texts the answer needs deposited for the two days?
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruments speak for the case` MEANS
        `is known` (`N 1 item 11(e) is named for the case` c)
    AND `is known` (`Rg 5 reg 65 gives the person the class licence for the case` c)
    AND ((NOT readings's `Rg 6 reg 22(1) Reading Y applies`) OR `is known` (`Rg 6 reg 22(1) dispenses with approval for the case` c))
    AND ((NOT readings's `s 95 Reading A applies`) OR `is known` (`the Broadcasting Act's answer` (`the Broadcasting Act's list for the case` c)))

-- the penalty of s 85 (s 65 of the 2000 Edition) as the version words it: before Act 10 of 2005 there is no further daily fine
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      o IS AN `Offence outcome`
GIVETH AN `Offence outcome`
`the outcome with the penalty of the version` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `an offence under` provision penalty THEN
        CONSIDER `the version of the Act for the case` c
        WHEN NOTHING THEN o
        WHEN JUST v THEN
            IF `TA versions: the general penalty has a further daily fine for a continuing offence` v
            THEN o
            ELSE `an offence under` provision (`Penalty` OF penalty's `fine not exceeding`, penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding, in months`, 0, penalty's `articles seized are forfeited in addition`)
    WHEN `no offence under this provision` THEN o

-- possession: s 54(2), with both readings of s 95 behind one switch
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH AN `Offence outcome`
`s 54(2) outcome before the version's penalty` MEANS
    IF readings's `s 95 Reading A applies`
    THEN `s 34(2) or s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A, in the text the version prints` (`the version of the Act for the case, or the 2020 text where none is known` c) (`the receiver as equipment` c) FALSE TRUE (`the held record` c readings) FALSE (`value of` (`the Broadcasting Act's answer` (`the Broadcasting Act's list for the case` c)))
    ELSE `s 34(2) or s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading B, in the text the version prints` (`the version of the Act for the case, or the 2020 text where none is known` c) (`the receiver as equipment` c) FALSE TRUE (`the held record` c readings)

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH AN `Offence outcome`
`s 54(2) outcome for the case` MEANS
    IF `the earlier wording of "equipment" leaves the receiver out` c readings
    THEN `no offence under this provision`
    ELSE `the outcome with the penalty of the version` c (`s 54(2) outcome before the version's penalty` c readings)

-- use: s 55(1), with the s 95 carve-out on Reading A.  A "use" is read as "operates" (s 55(1)).
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH AN `Offence outcome`
`s 55(1) outcome for the case` MEANS
    IF `the earlier wording of "equipment" leaves the receiver out` c readings
    THEN `no offence under this provision`
    ELSE IF (readings's `s 95 Reading A applies`) AND (`s 95: the Act does not apply to the licensing of this apparatus` (`value of` (`the Broadcasting Act's answer` (`the Broadcasting Act's list for the case` c))) FALSE FALSE)
         THEN `no offence under this provision`
         ELSE IF `s 35(1) or s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence, in the text the version prints` (`the version of the Act for the case, or the 2020 text where none is known` c) (`the receiver as equipment` c) TRUE `in a place in Singapore` (`the held record` c readings)
              THEN `the outcome with the penalty of the version` c (`an offence under` "section 55(1)" (`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` NOTHING))
              ELSE `no offence under this provision`

-- the two answers, for possession and for use
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`on the texts deposited: s 54(2) for the case` MEANS
    IF (`the text of the version is deposited for the case` c) AND (`the instruments speak for the case` c readings)
    THEN JUST (`s 54(2) outcome for the case` c readings)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`on the texts deposited: s 55(1) for the case` MEANS
    IF (`the text of the version is deposited for the case` c) AND (`the instruments speak for the case` c readings)
    THEN JUST (`s 55(1) outcome for the case` c readings)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- the days between the last deposited Act (Act 15 of 2017) and the deposited consolidation: the Act's own markers speak for ss 54, 55, 85, 95 and, per term, s 2 "equipment"
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      section IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the markers hold for the section on the conduct day` MEANS
        `value of` (`TA markers: on the markers, the deposited wording of the section was in force on the date` (c's `conduct day`) section)
    AND `value of` (`TA markers: on the markers, the deposited wording of the section was in force on the date` (c's `conduct day`) "85")
    AND `value of` (`TA markers: on the markers, the deposited wording of the section was in force on the date` (c's `conduct day`) "95")
    AND `value of` (`TA s 2 per-term markers: the deposited wording of the definition was in force on the date` (c's `conduct day`) "equipment")

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the case lies in the days after Act 15 of 2017 that no deposited Act covers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the Act for the case` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Revised Edition 2000` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `as amended by Act 10 of 2005` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `as amended by Act 19 of 2011` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `as amended by Act 22 of 2016` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `as amended by Act 30 of 2016` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `as amended by Act 15 of 2017` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO` THEN FALSE

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`also on the markers: s 54(2) for the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `on the texts deposited: s 54(2) for the case` c readings
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF (`the case lies in the days after Act 15 of 2017 that no deposited Act covers` c) AND (`the markers hold for the section on the conduct day` c "54") AND (`the instruments speak for the case` c readings)
        THEN JUST (`s 54(2) outcome for the case` c readings)
        ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`also on the markers: s 55(1) for the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `on the texts deposited: s 55(1) for the case` c readings
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF (`the case lies in the days after Act 15 of 2017 that no deposited Act covers` c) AND (`the markers hold for the section on the conduct day` c "55") AND (`the instruments speak for the case` c readings)
        THEN JUST (`s 55(1) outcome for the case` c readings)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- what the answer rests on, in words
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
GIVETH A STRING
`what the answer for the case rests on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the Act for the case` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "no version of the Act's text is published for that conduct day as read on that reading day"
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `Revised Edition 2000` THEN "the Revised Edition 2000, printed in the Gazette"
        WHEN `as amended by Act 10 of 2005` THEN "the Revised Edition 2000 as amended by Act 10 of 2005, both printed in the Gazette"
        WHEN `as amended by Act 19 of 2011` THEN "the Revised Edition 2000 as amended by Act 10 of 2005 and Act 19 of 2011 with its commencement notification S 33/2012, all printed in the Gazette"
        WHEN `as amended by Act 22 of 2016` THEN "the Revised Edition 2000 as amended by Acts 10 of 2005, 19 of 2011 and 22 of 2016, with the commencement notifications S 33/2012 and S 461/2016, all printed in the Gazette"
        WHEN `as amended by Act 30 of 2016` THEN "the Revised Edition 2000 as amended by Acts 10 of 2005, 19 of 2011, 22 of 2016 and 30 of 2016, with the commencement notifications S 33/2012, S 461/2016 and S 14/2017, all printed in the Gazette"
        WHEN `as amended by Act 15 of 2017` THEN "the Revised Edition 2000 as amended by Acts 10 of 2005, 19 of 2011, 22 of 2016, 30 of 2016 and 15 of 2017, all printed in the Gazette, with the commencement notifications S 33/2012, S 461/2016 and S 14/2017; Act 15 of 2017's own commencement notification is not deposited, so its day, 23 May 2017, is the Legislative History's"
        WHEN `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited` THEN "the Acts after Act 15 of 2017 are not wired into this version table (eight Acts and one Order are deposited as enacted, sgta-i-acts-after-2017.l4): only the Act's own amendment markers speak"
        WHEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO` THEN "the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from Singapore Statutes Online"

§ `1. Am I committing an offence by owning a receiver of broadcasts?`
-- Situation: none needed; every household with such a set may ask.

@export Am I committing an offence under the Telecommunications Act by owning (possessing) a receiver of broadcasts, for the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day? Answers only where the Act's text for that conduct day is deposited; otherwise NOTHING (the sources do not answer).
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day you ask about (the day of the conduct)
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at (for today's reading, today)
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
      `only receives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver only pick up signals and never send any?
      `picks up by radio waves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it pick up the broadcast signal as radio waves (through an aerial, antenna or dish) and not by cable?
      `holds a section 5 licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence of your own granted to you by the Authority under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act?
      `holds another authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a regulation or licence class under the Telecommunications Act that you can point to as covering you?
      `has a Minister's exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister exempted you, or people like you, from the Act under section 96?
      `holds a treaty licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence from another country that Singapore recognises under a treaty or arrangement (section 56)?
      `conforms to published standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver conform to technical standards that the Authority has published for equipment used for personal purposes?
      `localised on-site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you only use the receiver in one place, within your own premises?
      `only in a band the item authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the receiver only on radio frequencies that item 11 of the Exemption Notification's Schedule authorises (remote-control bands, not broadcast bands)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`Am I committing an offence by owning this receiver (on the texts deposited for the day)` MEANS
    `on the texts deposited: s 54(2) for the case` (`The case` OF (Date day month year), (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`), `kind of receiver`, `only receives`, `picks up by radio waves`, `holds a section 5 licence`, `holds another authorisation`, `has a Minister's exemption`, `holds a treaty licence`, `conforms to published standards`, `localised on-site`, `only in a band the item authorises`) `the default readings`

@export Am I committing an offence under the Telecommunications Act by owning (possessing) a receiver of broadcasts, for the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day, ALSO answering the days 1 Oct 2016 to 1 Oct 2026 from the deposited consolidation's own amendment markers? An inference from markers, not a text, for those days.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day you ask about (the day of the conduct)
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at (for today's reading, today)
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
      `only receives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver only pick up signals and never send any?
      `picks up by radio waves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it pick up the broadcast signal as radio waves (through an aerial, antenna or dish) and not by cable?
      `holds a section 5 licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence of your own granted to you by the Authority under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act?
      `holds another authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a regulation or licence class under the Telecommunications Act that you can point to as covering you?
      `has a Minister's exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister exempted you, or people like you, from the Act under section 96?
      `holds a treaty licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence from another country that Singapore recognises under a treaty or arrangement (section 56)?
      `conforms to published standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver conform to technical standards that the Authority has published for equipment used for personal purposes?
      `localised on-site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you only use the receiver in one place, within your own premises?
      `only in a band the item authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the receiver only on radio frequencies that item 11 of the Exemption Notification's Schedule authorises (remote-control bands, not broadcast bands)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`Am I committing an offence by owning this receiver (also on the Act's own amendment markers)` MEANS
    `also on the markers: s 54(2) for the case` (`The case` OF (Date day month year), (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`), `kind of receiver`, `only receives`, `picks up by radio waves`, `holds a section 5 licence`, `holds another authorisation`, `has a Minister's exemption`, `holds a treaty licence`, `conforms to published standards`, `localised on-site`, `only in a band the item authorises`) `the default readings`

§ `2. Am I committing an offence by switching it on and listening or watching?`

@export Am I committing an offence under the Telecommunications Act by switching on (operating) a receiver of broadcasts, for the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day? Answers only where the Act's text for that conduct day is deposited; otherwise NOTHING.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day you ask about (the day of the conduct)
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at (for today's reading, today)
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
      `only receives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver only pick up signals and never send any?
      `picks up by radio waves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it pick up the broadcast signal as radio waves (through an aerial, antenna or dish) and not by cable?
      `holds a section 5 licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence of your own granted to you by the Authority under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act?
      `holds another authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a regulation or licence class under the Telecommunications Act that you can point to as covering you?
      `has a Minister's exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister exempted you, or people like you, from the Act under section 96?
      `holds a treaty licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence from another country that Singapore recognises under a treaty or arrangement (section 56)?
      `conforms to published standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver conform to technical standards that the Authority has published for equipment used for personal purposes?
      `localised on-site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you only use the receiver in one place, within your own premises?
      `only in a band the item authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the receiver only on radio frequencies that item 11 of the Exemption Notification's Schedule authorises (remote-control bands, not broadcast bands)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`Am I committing an offence by switching this receiver on (on the texts deposited for the day)` MEANS
    `on the texts deposited: s 55(1) for the case` (`The case` OF (Date day month year), (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`), `kind of receiver`, `only receives`, `picks up by radio waves`, `holds a section 5 licence`, `holds another authorisation`, `has a Minister's exemption`, `holds a treaty licence`, `conforms to published standards`, `localised on-site`, `only in a band the item authorises`) `the default readings`

@export Am I committing an offence under the Telecommunications Act by switching on (operating) a receiver of broadcasts, for the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day, ALSO answering the days 1 Oct 2016 to 1 Oct 2026 from the deposited consolidation's own amendment markers? An inference from markers, not a text, for those days.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day you ask about (the day of the conduct)
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at (for today's reading, today)
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
      `only receives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver only pick up signals and never send any?
      `picks up by radio waves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it pick up the broadcast signal as radio waves (through an aerial, antenna or dish) and not by cable?
      `holds a section 5 licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence of your own granted to you by the Authority under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act?
      `holds another authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a regulation or licence class under the Telecommunications Act that you can point to as covering you?
      `has a Minister's exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister exempted you, or people like you, from the Act under section 96?
      `holds a treaty licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence from another country that Singapore recognises under a treaty or arrangement (section 56)?
      `conforms to published standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver conform to technical standards that the Authority has published for equipment used for personal purposes?
      `localised on-site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you only use the receiver in one place, within your own premises?
      `only in a band the item authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the receiver only on radio frequencies that item 11 of the Exemption Notification's Schedule authorises (remote-control bands, not broadcast bands)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`Am I committing an offence by switching this receiver on (also on the Act's own amendment markers)` MEANS
    `also on the markers: s 55(1) for the case` (`The case` OF (Date day month year), (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`), `kind of receiver`, `only receives`, `picks up by radio waves`, `holds a section 5 licence`, `holds another authorisation`, `has a Minister's exemption`, `holds a treaty licence`, `conforms to published standards`, `localised on-site`, `only in a band the item authorises`) `the default readings`

§ `3. What does the answer rest on, and what does the Broadcasting Act's list say?`

@export What does the Telecommunications Act answer for this conduct day, as read on this reading day, rest on: a printed text, the markers of the deposited consolidation, or nothing?
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day you ask about (the day of the conduct)
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at (for today's reading, today)
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
      `only receives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver only pick up signals and never send any?
      `picks up by radio waves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it pick up the broadcast signal as radio waves (through an aerial, antenna or dish) and not by cable?
      `holds a section 5 licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence of your own granted to you by the Authority under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act?
      `holds another authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a regulation or licence class under the Telecommunications Act that you can point to as covering you?
      `has a Minister's exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister exempted you, or people like you, from the Act under section 96?
      `holds a treaty licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence from another country that Singapore recognises under a treaty or arrangement (section 56)?
      `conforms to published standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the receiver conform to technical standards that the Authority has published for equipment used for personal purposes?
      `localised on-site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you only use the receiver in one place, within your own premises?
      `only in a band the item authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the receiver only on radio frequencies that item 11 of the Exemption Notification's Schedule authorises (remote-control bands, not broadcast bands)?
GIVETH A STRING
`What does the answer rest on` MEANS
    `what the answer for the case rests on` (`The case` OF (Date day month year), (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`), `kind of receiver`, `only receives`, `picks up by radio waves`, `holds a section 5 licence`, `holds another authorisation`, `has a Minister's exemption`, `holds a treaty licence`, `conforms to published standards`, `localised on-site`, `only in a band the item authorises`)

@export Does the First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act 1994 list this kind of receiver, for the conduct day, as the First Schedule is read on the reading day?
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day of the conduct
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
GIVETH A `Is the receiver on the Broadcasting Act list`
`Does the First Schedule list this kind of receiver` MEANS
    `the First Schedule lists the kind of receiver, for the conduct day as read on the reading day` `kind of receiver` (Date day month year) (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`)

@export Were the Broadcasting Act's television and radio licensing regulations (Rg 1) in operation for the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day? This says whether the regulations existed, not what they required: they were amended on 21 June 2004 (S 333/2004), and the next question says what each version required. NOTHING before 29 February 2004 (no earlier edition is deposited).
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day of the conduct
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Were the receiver licensing regulations in operation` MEANS
    `Rg 1, the television and radio licensing regulations, are in operation for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date day month year) (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`)

@export What did the Broadcasting Act's television and radio licensing regulations (Rg 1) say in terms about a licence for this kind of receiver in this place, in the version that applies to the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day? Three versions: the Revised Edition 2004 (from 29 February 2004), as amended by S 333/2004 (from 21 June 2004, published 15 June 2004), and revoked by S 548/2012 (from 1 January 2011, published 31 October 2012). The answer names the regulation and quotes it, or says no regulation of the version says so in terms; the Broadcasting Act's own section 20(1) is not a regulation and is not in the answer.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day of the conduct
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
      `kind of receiver` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc Is it a television, an FM radio, an AM radio, or a satellite dish system?
      `place of the receiver` IS A `Place of the receiver` @desc Is it in a house or flat, in a vehicle, in a vessel that has no ship station licence, or in a commercial property?
GIVETH A STRING
`What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` MEANS
    `what Rg 1 says in terms about a licence for the kind of receiver in the place, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day` `kind of receiver` `place of the receiver` (Date day month year) (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`)

§ `4. What is the most I can be punished with?`

@export What is the most I can be punished with if I am convicted of an offence under section 54 or 55 of the Telecommunications Act, which state no penalty of their own? This is the general penalty of section 85 (section 65 of the 2000 Revised Edition) for the conduct day, as the law is read on the reading day; NOTHING where no deposited text speaks.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day of the conduct
      month IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day of the conduct
      year IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day of the conduct
      `reading day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day the law is read as at
      `reading month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the day the law is read as at
      `reading year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day the law is read as at
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Penalty`)
`What is the most I can be punished with` MEANS
    CONSIDER `TA versions: the version of the Act's text that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date day month year) (Date `reading day` `reading month` `reading year`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        IF NOT (`TA versions: the text of the version is deposited` v)
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `TA versions: the general penalty has a further daily fine for a continuing offence` v
             THEN JUST (`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` NOTHING)
             ELSE JUST (`Penalty` OF 10000, 36, 0, TRUE)

@export May an offence under section 54 or 55 be settled by paying a sum instead of going to court, and for how much at most? Asks about a sum asked of you and whether the offence is prescribed as compoundable; the ceiling in section 84(1) is $5,000, as the deposited current text states it.
GIVEN `the sum asked of me` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum an authorised officer asks you to pay to settle the offence, in dollars
      `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed this offence as one that may be compounded (by regulations made with the Minister's approval)?
      `the officer is specially authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a police officer of at least the rank of sergeant specially authorised by name by the Minister, or an employee of the Authority specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I settle by paying a sum` MEANS
    `s 84(1): the offence may be compounded for this sum` `the sum asked of me` `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` `the officer is specially authorised`

§ `5. What turns on the readings?`

-- Every combination of the four readings, for the same facts.  A person does not choose a reading; a court does.
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      readings IS A `Readings applied`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
`What turns on the readings (possession, on the texts deposited for the day)` MEANS
    `on the texts deposited: s 54(2) for the case` c readings

§ `6. Interpretation Act s 9A: is the literal answer in the territory the section names?`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 s 9A (encoded at subjects/sg/interpretation-act/encodings/legalese-sonnet-5.5/; cited, not re-encoded; no code link).
-- s 9A(1): a court may prefer the purposive reading.  s 9A(2): extrinsic material (Hansard, the Gazette, a Bill's explanatory statement) may be looked at to
-- confirm the ordinary meaning, or, where the ordinary meaning is ambiguous or obscure, or leads to a result that is manifestly
-- absurd or unreasonable (s 9A(2)(b)(ii)), to find the meaning.  Whether the second condition is met is the court's, so it is an
-- input.  THIS FUNCTION NEVER CHANGES THE LITERAL ANSWER: it echoes it, unchanged, beside the weighing.
GIVEN `the literal answer` IS A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
      `a court finds the ordinary meaning ambiguous or obscure, or the literal result manifestly absurd or unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 9A weighing`
`s 9A: the weighing of the literal answer` MEANS
    `s 9A weighing` OF `the literal answer`
        , (   `a court finds the ordinary meaning ambiguous or obscure, or the literal result manifestly absurd or unreasonable`
           AND `is an offence` `the literal answer`)

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE (`Offence outcome`)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST o THEN
        CONSIDER o
        WHEN `an offence under` provision penalty THEN TRUE
        WHEN `no offence under this provision` THEN FALSE
